<title>UK: SOCCER-MIDDLESBROUGH FACE F.A. INQUIRY.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-MIDDLESBROUGH FACE F.A. INQUIRY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Middlesbrough must face the English F.A. on January 14 after being charged with a breach of premier league rules for calling off last Saturday's match against Blackburn Rovers without permission.</p>
<p>Middlesbrough postponed the fixture because of an injury list and outbreak of influenza which they said deprived them of 23 players.</p>
<p>There are no precedents for such a case but the club could be fined and lose league points.</p>
</text>
